### Enterprise Backend API Examples
### Use with REST Client extension in VS Code or any HTTP client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@contentType = application/json

### Variables (will be set from responses)
@accessToken = 
@refreshToken = 

###############################################################################
### HEALTH CHECKS
###############################################################################

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Database Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/db

###############################################################################
### AUTHENTICATION - SIGN UP
###############################################################################

### Sign Up - Create new user account
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "username": "johndoe",
  "password": "SecurePass123",
  "full_name": "John Doe"
}

### Sign Up - Another user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "username": "janesmith",
  "password": "AnotherSecure456",
  "full_name": "Jane Smith"
}

### Sign Up - Duplicate Email (will fail with 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "username": "different_username",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Sign Up - Weak Password (will fail with 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "weak@example.com",
  "username": "weakuser",
  "password": "weak"
}

###############################################################################
### AUTHENTICATION - LOGIN
###############################################################################

### Login - Get access token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Extract tokens from login response (for REST Client)
# After running login, these will be available
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}

### Login - Invalid credentials (will fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### Login - Non-existent user (will fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "SomePassword123"
}

###############################################################################
### AUTHENTICATED ENDPOINTS
###############################################################################

### Get Current User Info (Authenticate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Verify Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get Current User - Invalid Token (will fail with 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here

### Get Current User - No Token (will fail with 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

###############################################################################
### TOKEN REFRESH
###############################################################################

### Refresh Access Token
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Update access token from refresh response
@accessToken = {{refresh.response.body.access_token}}

### Refresh Token - Invalid token (will fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refresh_token": "invalid_refresh_token"
}

###############################################################################
### EXAMPLE WORKFLOW
###############################################################################

### Complete Authentication Flow:
### 1. Sign up to create account
### 2. Login to get tokens
### 3. Use access token for authenticated requests
### 4. When access token expires, use refresh token
### 5. Continue using new access token

###############################################################################
### TESTING DIFFERENT SCENARIOS
###############################################################################

### Sign Up - Admin User (will be created as STAFF by default)
# To make this user an ADMIN, you need to manually update the database:
# UPDATE users SET role = 'ADMIN' WHERE email = 'admin@example.com';
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "AdminPass123",
  "full_name": "System Administrator"
}

### Sign Up - Minimal Data
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "minimal@example.com",
  "username": "minimaluser",
  "password": "MinimalPass123"
}

### Sign Up - Special Characters in Username (will fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "special@example.com",
  "username": "user@name!",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Sign Up - Email Format Invalid (will fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

###############################################################################
### NOTES
###############################################################################

# Password Requirements:
# - Minimum 8 characters
# - At least one uppercase letter
# - At least one lowercase letter
# - At least one digit

# Username Requirements:
# - 3-50 characters
# - Alphanumeric characters and underscores only
# - Automatically converted to lowercase

# Token Expiration:
# - Access Token: 30 minutes (configurable)
# - Refresh Token: 7 days (configurable)

# User Roles:
# - STAFF: Default role, standard permissions
# - ADMIN: Administrative privileges (must be set manually)

# HTTP Status Codes:
# - 200: Success (Login, Get User)
# - 201: Created (Sign Up)
# - 400: Bad Request
# - 401: Unauthorized (Invalid credentials/token)
# - 403: Forbidden (No token provided)
# - 409: Conflict (Email/username exists)
# - 422: Validation Error
# - 500: Internal Server Error
